## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the six; `web/package.json` changed in any line other than the one undici pin, or the pin not exactly `7.30.1` (a range, a caret, another major); a lockfile line beyond the zod and undici entries; any `run:` line or step key (other than the one `name:`) changed in `ci.yml`; a changed audit mechanism line; a word added to a product surface; a removed test name beyond the declared rename, a skip, `.only`, environment gate or sleep in an added row; **Mg or Mg2 surviving (a re-added exception goes unseen)**; **the head or merge ref still FAILING on a zod or braces finding at your clock**; **any PR check-run failed whose cause you have not read, or either `api on SQL Server` shard not `completed` `success`** (a check-run red because of a base fact OTHER than zod or undici, proven by the same output on `-base` and on main's latest `web build`, is a Major `CI red: base fact`, not a Blocker; **a production-audit or dev-audit failure on undici or zod at the SUBJECT HEAD is a Blocker**, and a `web build` step 5 or 6 not green at the SUBJECT HEAD is a Blocker until its cause is read); a raw non-ASCII byte in an added line; a ticket key, card id or person name in an added line or commit message; a secret; a new open alert; the head moved. *Major:* a non-equivalent mutant surviving (M1-M4, Mu, Mx, Mn); a builder claim contradicted at its OWN clock (2666 -> 2668, 0 names lost beyond the rename, 13 rows, 4 of 4 killed, B571's lock diff = zod only at `df464e51` and `package.json` untouched there, 50 repeats red 0; B579's one-line package.json diff, undici-only lock entries and consumer list); a new or re-aimed row that no mutant turns red and is not a declared control; a repeat red; the CI-red-on-base-fact above; an undici behaviour change that reaches the BFF's `Agent` use and B579 did not name; the builder's rc 0 audit claim read wrong because you did not record the clock; the comment sentence 'no fixed braces shipped' false. *Minor/Note:* a builder claim